{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3212","published":"2026-08-01T11:12:05Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:25.928950815Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-54466"],"summary":"nodejs-websocket-driver security update","details":".\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nwebsocket-driver is a WebSocket protocol handler with pluggable I/O. Prior to 0.7.5, the frame format in draft versions of the WebSocket protocol includes a length header that allows an arbitrarily large integer to be encoded as a sequence of bytes with the high bit set. By sending an indefinite sequence of bytes with values 0x80 or above, a client can make the server parse these bytes into an ever-growing integer in lib/websocket/driver/draft75.js; because JavaScript numbers are 64-bit floating point values, this number will eventually lose precision and lead to the subsequent payload being parsed incorrectly. This issue is fixed in version 0.7.5.(CVE-2026-54466)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nodejs-websocket-driver","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nodejs-websocket-driver&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.3.3-2.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"noarch":["nodejs-websocket-driver-0.3.3-2.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["nodejs-websocket-driver-0.3.3-2.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3212.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-websocket-driver","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nodejs-websocket-driver&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.3.3-2.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"noarch":["nodejs-websocket-driver-0.3.3-2.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["nodejs-websocket-driver-0.3.3-2.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3212.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-websocket-driver","ecosys